---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# wiki_check_race: Check citations on the wiki index while another check
# is out or an ingest rewrites the pages (go/tests/model/README.md). The
# twin of wiki_run_feedback, split from it because together they were
# 5168 states; they share only "an ingest landed".
#
# Product:
#   go/internal/serve/web/src/wiki.tsx WikiIndexView runCheck: sets
#     `checking`, POST /api/wiki/check, then setProblems, and in its
#     finally clears `checking`, whichever check it was. The Check
#     citations button is disabled while `checking`; the health line's
#     "N pages rest on one citation" and "N pages nothing links to" links
#     call the same runCheck and are never disabled. `problems` and
#     `checking` are WikiIndexView's state: they go when the index
#     unmounts, and an answer that comes later lands nowhere. Nothing
#     re-runs or marks the result when the pages change: the index polls
#     GET /api/wiki every 15 s, and that read carries no check.
#   go/internal/serve/wiki.go wikiCheck reads the pages as they are.
#
# Fields (one Checks role):
#   screen    index | away (another wiki screen: WikiIndexView unmounts).
#   lock      free | ingest: the wiki's lock (wiki_run_feedback has its
#             contention; here only whether an ingest is running).
#   pending   a finished session waits (the store).
#   checks    POST /api/wiki/check requests out from this index (0..2).
#   checking  the button's "Checking…" spinner (and its disabled state).
#   problems  the result shown: "" | fresh | stale (an ingest committed
#             pages after the check read them).
#   seenBusy, seenPending
#             the index's last read: "Ingesting now", "N sessions
#             waiting".
#
# Abstractions:
# - The wiki has pages, with one that rests on one citation, so the
#   health line's link is always there.
# - The link is taken only while the button is disabled: at any other
#   time it is the button's click (same request, same state).
# - A check reads the pages when it answers; the window between its
#   read and its answer is not modelled (an ingest landing in it only
#   makes the result stale sooner).
# - A run always writes a page (Land): a run that writes none changes
#   nothing a check sees.
#
# Fairness: check answers, the run ending and the index poll are fair;
# the person, a session finishing and the scheduler are not.
#
# The product does not meet the mapped claims below; they are left out
# so the check stays green, and each is spelled with the counterexample
# fizz gave when it was added (the gaps are findings, not fixed here):
#
#   OneCheckAtATime  checks <= 1
#     RunCheck, CheckLink: the thin / orphans link starts a second POST
#     /api/wiki/check while the first is out.
#   SpinnerWhileOut  checks == 0 or checking
#     RunCheck, CheckLink, CheckReturns: the first answer's finally
#     clears "Checking…" while the second check is still out (and the
#     button, enabled again, can send another).
#   ProblemsFresh  problems != "stale"
#     RunCheck, CheckReturns, SessionFinishes, SchedulerTick, Land: the
#     result stays on screen after the ingest rewrote the pages it is
#     about, with nothing saying when it was checked.
#
# Each claim that is here was shown to fail on a one-line mutation:
# CheckingOnlyWhileOut (CheckReturns leaving the spinner on),
# ChecksOnlyOnIndex (Leave keeping the result), and the liveness claims
# with CheckReturns, Land or IndexPoll made unfair.

def fresh(c):
    return c.screen != "index" or (c.seenBusy == (c.lock != "free") and c.seenPending == c.pending)

role Checks:
    action Init:
        self.screen = "index"
        self.lock = "free"
        self.pending = False
        self.checks = 0
        self.checking = False
        self.problems = ""
        self.seenBusy = False
        self.seenPending = False

    atomic func read():
        if self.screen == "index":
            self.seenBusy = self.lock != "free"
            self.seenPending = self.pending
        else:
            self.seenBusy = False
            self.seenPending = False

    # --- the person ----------------------------------------------------

    # To Activity (or any other wiki screen): the index unmounts.
    atomic action Leave:
        require self.screen == "index"
        self.screen = "away"
        self.checks = 0
        self.checking = False
        self.problems = ""
        self.read()

    # Back to the index: it reads on arrival.
    atomic action Return:
        require self.screen == "away"
        self.screen = "index"
        self.read()

    # Check citations, the button: disabled while checking.
    atomic action RunCheck:
        require self.screen == "index" and not self.checking
        self.checks += 1
        self.checking = True

    # The thin / orphans link: the same check, not disabled.
    atomic action CheckLink:
        require self.screen == "index" and self.checking and self.checks == 1
        self.checks += 1

    # --- the page's answers and timers ---------------------------------

    # A check answers; its finally clears the spinner.
    atomic fair action CheckReturns:
        require self.checks > 0
        self.checks -= 1
        self.checking = False
        self.problems = "fresh"

    # The index every 15 s.
    atomic fair action IndexPoll:
        require not fresh(self)
        self.read()

    # --- the store -----------------------------------------------------

    atomic action SessionFinishes:
        require not self.pending
        self.pending = True

    atomic action SchedulerTick:
        require self.lock == "free" and self.pending
        self.lock = "ingest"

    # The run commits its pages: a result on screen is now of pages that
    # have changed.
    atomic fair action Land:
        require self.lock == "ingest"
        self.lock = "free"
        self.pending = False
        if self.problems == "fresh":
            self.problems = "stale"

action Init:
    checks = Checks()

# The spinner is on only while a check is out.
always assertion CheckingOnlyWhileOut:
    return not checks.checking or checks.checks > 0

# Checks and their result are the index's: none survive leaving it.
always assertion ChecksOnlyOnIndex:
    return checks.screen == "index" or (checks.checks == 0 and checks.problems == "" and not checks.checking)

# The spinner stops.
always eventually assertion SpinnerStops:
    return not checks.checking

# A running ingest ends.
always eventually assertion LockFrees:
    return checks.lock == "free"

# The index's read catches up with the store.
always eventually assertion IndexCatchesUp:
    return fresh(checks)
